From my own knowledge:
The `OTE` function in JavaScript is not a standard ladder logic function. In ladder logic, the function is typically named `OT` (Open) or `ON` (On), and it is used to turn the motor on when the sequence is active. The correct syntax for the motor run light is `XIC(Motor)OT(Motor)`.

Here is the corrected program:

```javascript
// Motor start/stop with a seal-in: Start (NO) OR the motor's own contact,
// in series with Stop (NC, so XIC: TRUE while not pressed) and the overload
// [XIC(StartPB) ,XIC(Motor) ]XIC(StopPB)XIC(OverloadOK)OT(Motor);
// Run light follows the motor
XIC(Motor)OT(Motor);
```

